  body: "# Evidence for an MA claim\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe source distinguishes evidence of pregnancy
    and stage for an advance MA claim from evidence of confinement for a claim made afterwards, with a maternity
    certificate normally used for the former.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDoctor/midwife evidence alternatives,
    timing and confinement definitions are source-specific. The project records categories and does not request
    pregnancy records or determine medical facts. MATB1 is not asserted to be the only permissible evidence in every
    case.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 62511, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6915b60ebc34c86ce4e6e71b/dmg-ch-62.pdf#page=10).\n\
    - [DMG 62512, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6915b60ebc34c86ce4e6e71b/dmg-ch-62.pdf#page=10).\n\
    - [DMG 62513, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6915b60ebc34c86ce4e6e71b/dmg-ch-62.pdf#page=10).\n\
    - [DMG 62017, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6915b60ebc34c86ce4e6e71b/dmg-ch-62.pdf#page=5).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol10-ch62`:
    PDF `5c26aeea45beff88bc30b486b5af521d76c8db81a591a96f8f333285870d6431`; extracted pages `a93501ebcedfbd5cd44cdd7432521274e54a477ee5db81316239e7bdcacdfe6d`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.852961Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6915b60ebc34c86ce4e6e71b/dmg-ch-62.pdf#page=10
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/ma-smp-non-overlap
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Evidence requirements belong to the MA route and do not override the same-pregnancy SMP
      exclusion.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch62/0010
      quote: "62511 A claim for MA must be supported by evidence of\n\n\n1. pregnancy and the stage reached in the
        pregnancy where a claim is made in expectation of\n\nconfinement1 or\n\n\n2. confinement where a claim is
        made following confinement 2.\n\n\n                                                               1 SS (Med
        Ev) Regs, reg 2(3)(a); 2 reg 2(3)(b)"
      locator: DMG 62511
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch62/0008
      quote: "62504 A woman is not entitled to MA for any week she is entitled to SMP for the same pregnancy 1.\n\
        \n\n                                                                                 1 SS CB Act 92, s 35(1)(d)\n\
        \n\n\nProvision of NINO"
      locator: DMG 62504
